Subject: [PATCH] A cabinet-link command stops attract mode

The link only acts while the menu stands still, and attract mode keeps it moving: the touch-screen
search took longer than the attract timeout to type, and every "goto" it sent was dropped. A
command that arrives while the menu is busy now stops attract; the helper's resend then lands.
---
diff --git a/RetroFE/Source/RetroFE.cpp b/RetroFE/Source/RetroFE.cpp
index 11b6040..b520761 100644
--- a/RetroFE/Source/RetroFE.cpp
+++ b/RetroFE/Source/RetroFE.cpp
@@ -752,7 +752,9 @@ void RetroFE::linkPoll() {
 
 	std::string cmd;
 	while (link.receive(cmd)) {
-		if (!still || kioskLock_) continue;                    // busy: the command is dropped, the helper sends again
+		// ArcadeMaster: attract mode keeps the menu moving, so a command never found it standing still (the touch search
+		// typed for 20 s and its pick was dropped every time): a command stops attract, the helper's resend then lands
+		if (!still || kioskLock_) { if (!kioskLock_) attract_.reset(); continue; }   // busy: dropped, the helper sends again
 		std::vector<std::string> p;
 		std::stringstream ss(cmd); std::string part;
 		while (std::getline(ss, part, '\t')) p.push_back(part);
